{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>This is what HaShem spoke, saying: I will be sanctified through those near to Me.</b> Rashi explained: and where did He speak? ״וְנִקְדַּשׁ בִּכְבוֹדִי״ (Exodus 29:43) — do not read בִּכְבוֹדִי but rather בִּמְכֻבָּדַי, 'through those who are honored by Me.' But there is no need for this, for it is already stated here: ״וְעַל פְּנֵי כָל הָעָם אֶכָּבֵד,״ if so the meaning of the verse is thus: ״וְנִקְדַּשׁ״ — that is, the House would be sanctified through a matter that is My glory, for through it I will be honored before all the people, and this can only be through those near to HaShem, blessed be He. For all who are near — the one who draws nearer to HaShem, blessed be He, more than others — from him all those lesser than him will learn an a fortiori argument (קַל וָחֹמֶר), saying: if fire seized the moist branches, what will the dry thorns do? And then they will all take reproof. And this is the glory of HaShem, blessed be He, before all the people." "And this is what Rashi explained: Moses said to Aaron, 'Aaron my brother, I knew that the House would be sanctified through the intimates (מְיֻדָּעָיו) of the Omnipresent, and I supposed it would be either through me or through you. Now I see that they are greater than me and you.' And by what was it known that they were greater? Rather, surely the explanation of the matter is thus: the Holy One, blessed be He, grasps two extremes. One extreme is that the Holy One, blessed be He, is exacting with the righteous more than with those lesser than them; the second extreme is that He punishes them even for a minor error — and all this so that from them an a fortiori argument (קַל וָחֹמֶר) may be learned, as mentioned, by all those lesser than they — an a fortiori argument that they could not have learned if He had punished some average person, or if He had punished him for some great transgression. And the verse says ״וְעַל פְּנֵי כָל הָעָם אֶכָּבֵד,״ meaning that they will all be careful with My honor from now on, for they will all take reproof from this a fortiori argument; and if they were not greater even than me, then this reproof would not reach them all, for those greater than they would say, 'the harm will not reach us,' and this reproof would be taken only by those lesser than they. And even to those equal to them in rank it would not reach, for each one would err and say, 'I am greater than my fellow' — except for one about whom all agree that he is greater than them all; from him reproof is taken by all. And this is the essence of sanctification of the Name, for from then on they will fear HaShem, His holy ones, as it says (Psalms 89:8). And this is what it says: ״בִּקְרֹבַי אֶקָּדֵשׁ״ — in the one who is near to Me more than his fellow, in him I will be sanctified, for through him, ״עַל פְּנֵי כָל הָעָם אֶכָּבֵד,״ the reproof will reach them all. And this is what is said (Leviticus 16:1): ״בְּקָרְבָתָם לִפְנֵי ה׳ וַיָּמֻתוּ״ — because they were near to HaShem more than others, therefore ״וַיָּמֻתוּ״." "And this is the reason for ״וַתֹּאכַל בִּקְצֵה הַמַּחֲנֶה,״ which our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (Yalkut Shimoni 732) as 'בִּקְצִינִים שֶׁבַּמַּחֲנֶה' — among the wicked of the camp; and as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Bava Qamma 60a): 'Punishment does not come to the world except on account of the wicked, but it does not begin except with the righteous,' etc. And the explanation of the matter is that it begins with the righteous precisely so that the wicked will take reproof. And this is what it says: ״וַאֲחֵיכֶם כָּל בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל יִבְכּוּ״ and so on — they will fear and be afraid for themselves lest what happened to these happen to them, when they see that HaShem does not show favor to anyone. And this is a precious interpretation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The verse וְעַל פְּנֵי כָל הָעָם אֶכָּבֵד is from Exodus, cited here implicitly; the phrase about fire and thorns is an allusion to the Talmudic idiom (Mo'ed Qatan 25a)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:35:37.561683593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}